		"note": "An example cannot add a member without leaving a fourth one behind for every later example, so this shows the two things the add is built out of. `POST /v3/cluster/member/add` with `{\"peerURLs\":[\"http://...\"]}` answers with the new member's id and the list it now belongs to, and only then is the process started, with `--initial-cluster-state existing` and an `--initial-cluster` naming all four. Starting it first, or leaving that flag off, bootstraps a second cluster that will never merge with this one.",
